  "description": "This derivative dataset provides preprocessed stereo-EEG (SEEG) high-gamma power from 16 patients performing a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment conditions. Power was computed from bipolar derivations using multitaper analysis and time-locked to outcome at 256 Hz. Trial-wise behavioural variables and anatomical labels accompany the signals, supporting study of frontal cortex interactions in reward and punishment learning.",
  "methods_description": "High-gamma power was computed from bipolar SEEG derivations using multitaper estimation, time-locked to outcome (-0.5 to 1.5 s, 256 Hz). The released trial arrays were repackaged into BrainVision float32 format, with behaviour and anatomy tables converted into events and channels TSV files.",
